users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87IuCDm\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4038300849,\"number\":190,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"ci: fix push_repo_memory spawnSync ENOBUFS on large repo\",\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\n`push_repo_memory` was failing with `spawnSync git ENOBUFS` when the `memory/audit-workflows` branch didn't yet exist. The internal `push_repo_memory.cjs` script took the orphan-branch path: `git checkout --orphan` followed by `git rm -rf .` — on this repo's ~217k-file working tree, that command's output overflows Node.js's `spawnSync` 1 MB buffer.\\n\\n**Fix:** Add an \\\"Ensure memory branch exists\\\" step in the `push_repo_memory` job in `audit-workflows.lock.yml`, before the push step, that pre-creates `memory/audit-workflows` via the GitHub REST API when it doesn't exist:\\n\\n1. `POST /git/trees` — tree with a single `.gitkeep` file (`{\\\"tree\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\".gitkeep\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"100644\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"blob\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"\\\"}]}`)\\n2. `POST /git/commits` — root commit, no parents\\n3. `POST /git/refs` — create `refs/heads/memory/audit-workflows`\\n\\nThis forces `push_repo_memory.cjs` to always take the existing-branch path (fetch → checkout → diff → push), bypassing the orphan creation entirely.\\n\\n**Note on tree creation:** The GitHub REST API rejects an empty tree `{\\\"tree\\\":[]}` with HTTP 422 \\\"Invalid tree info\\\". The tree must contain at least one entry, so a single empty `.gitkeep` file is used.\\n\\n**Why the fix is in `audit-workflows.lock.yml` rather than the `.md` source:** gh-aw v0.53.6 provides no frontmatter mechanism to inject steps into the auto-generated `push_repo_memory` job. All alternatives were verified and blocked:\\n- `steps:` / `post-steps:` inject into the agent job, which cannot have `contents: write` (blocked by gh-aw's security enforcement even with `strict: false`)\\n- `safe-outputs: steps:` injects only into the `safe_outputs` job, not `push_repo_memory`\\n- `jobs:` custom entries cannot override auto-generated jobs (error: \\\"job already exists\\\") and are not added to `push_repo_memory`'s `needs:` automatically\\n\\nThe lock.yml edit is accompanied by a detailed `# INTENTIONAL MANUAL EDIT` comment explaining the constraint and when re-application is needed. The `audit-workflows.md` \\\"Large-Repository Compatibility\\\" section and `.github/copilot-instructions.md` are updated to document this intentional exception.\\n\\n**Note:** Once the `memory/audit-workflows` branch exists after the first successful run, subsequent runs — including runs from a freshly compiled lock.yml — will work without this step. The step only needs to be re-applied if `gh aw compile` is run while the branch doesn't exist.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nValidated YAML syntax with `python3 -c \\\"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(...)\\\"`. The step is idempotent — if the branch already exists, it logs and skips. All gh-aw frontmatter alternatives were compiled and tested to confirm they are not viable. The initial fix was tested against a live CI run (run 22798555427) which revealed the empty-tree HTTP 422 error; the corrected tree payload was confirmed to be the appropriate fix.\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ----\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_title\\u003e[aw] Agentic Workflow Audit Agent failed\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_description\\u003e### Workflow Failure\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e **Workflow:** [Agentic Workflow Audit Agent](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/[REDACTED]/.github/workflows/audit-workflows.md)  \\n\\u003e **Branch:** 13.3.rel1  \\n\\u003e **Run:** https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e **⚠️ Repo-Memory Push Failed**: The push-repo-memory job failed to write memory back to the repository. This may indicate a permission issue, a configuration error, or a network problem. Check the [workflow run](https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711) for details.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ### Action Required\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e **Option 1: Assign this issue to Copilot**\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Assign this issue to Copilot using the `agentic-workflows` sub-agent to automatically debug and fix the workflow failure.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e **Option 2: Manually invoke the agent**\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Debug this workflow failure using your favorite Agent CLI and the `agentic-workflows` prompt.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - Start your agent\\n\\u003e - Load the `agentic-workflows` prompt from `.github/agents/agentic-workflows.agent.md` or \\u003chttps://github.com/github/gh-aw/blob/main/.github/agents/agentic-workflows.agent.md\\u003e\\n\\u003e - Type `debug the agentic workflow audit-workflows failure in https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711`\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003e Generated from [Agentic Workflow Audit Agent](https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711)\\n\\u003e \\u003e - [x] expires \\u003c!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-13T22:12:07.946Z --\\u003e on Mar 13, 2026, 10:12 PM UTC\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Agentic Workflow Audit Agent, gh-aw-tracker-id: audit-workflows-daily, id: 22783839711, workflow_id: audit-workflows, run: https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711 --\\u003e\\u003c/issue_description\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003ccomments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/comments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003e **Custom agent used: agentic-workflows**\\n\\u003e GitHub Agentic Workflows (gh-aw) - Create, debug, and upgrade AI-powered workflows with intelligent prompt routing\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX --\\u003e\\n\\n- Fixes grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32#189\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS --\\u003e\\n---\\n\\n🔒 GitHub Advanced Security automatically protects Copilot coding agent pull requests. You can protect all pull requests by enabling Advanced Security for your repositories. [Learn more about Advanced Security.](https://gh.io/cca-advanced-security)\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},\"comments\":4,\"closed_at\":\"2026-03-07T17:41:18Z\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-07T11:45:19Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-07T17:41:19Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/190\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/190\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/190/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/190/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/190/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32\",\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/190\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/190\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-o