d}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87ItfiL\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4038287891,\"number\":188,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"fix: increase daily-test-improver repo-memory max-file-size to 10 MiB\",\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\nThe Daily Test Improver `push_repo_memory` job was failing because `build-common.sh` (12 KiB) exceeded the default 10 KiB per-file size limit, causing the entire memory write to abort.\\n\\n- **`daily-test-improver.md`**: Replace `repo-memory: true` with explicit `max-file-size: 102400` (100 KiB), matching the limit already used by `audit-workflows.md`\\n- **`daily-test-improver.lock.yml`**: Update `MAX_FILE_SIZE` and `MAX_PATCH_SIZE` from `10240` → `102400` to match\\n- **`daily-test-improver.lock.yml`**: Update `GH_AW_MEMORY_CONSTRAINTS` string to advertise the actual configured limits (`102400 bytes / 100 KiB`), replacing the stale `10240 bytes` values that no longer matched\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nValidated against the failing run ([#22793310237](https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22793310237)) — error was `build-common.sh (12066 bytes \\u003e 10240 bytes)`, which the increased limit resolves.\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ----\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\