01?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87Irnus\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4036597431,\"number\":180,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"feat: initialise gh-aw agents\",\"body\":\"---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003e [!IMPORTANT]\\r\\n\\u003e **PR title must follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format.**\\r\\n\\u003e\\r\\n\\u003e PRs are squashed into the target branch using the **PR title** as the commit message.\\r\\n\\u003e The PR title must therefore conform to commitlint requirements:\\r\\n\\u003e\\r\\n\\u003e ```\\r\\n\\u003e \\u003ctype\\u003e[(optional scope)][!]: \\u003cdescription\\u003e\\r\\n\\u003e ```\\r\\n\\u003e\\r\\n\\u003e Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`\\r\\n\\u003e\\r\\n\\u003e Examples: `feat: add ARMv8-M support`, `fix: correct stack calculation`, `docs: update build instructions`\\r\\n\\u003e\\r\\n\\u003e Individual commits **within** the PR do **not** need to follow this format.\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"COLLABORATOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"},\"comments\":0,\"closed_at\":\"2026-03-07T09:15:11Z\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-06T23:17:52Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-07T09:15:11Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/180\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/180\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/180/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/180/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/180/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32\",\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/180\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/180\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/180.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/180.patch\",\"merged_at\":\"2026-03-07T09:15:10Z\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/180/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87In8ts\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4035567494,\"number\":175,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"ci: add merge_group trigger to all CI workflows and update commitlint for merge queue\",\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\nAdds merge queue (`merge_group`) support across all CI workflows so required checks run when a PR enters the queue. Updates `commitlint` to validate the squash commit message in the merge queue context. Cache writes are made read-only for `merge_group` events to avoid polluting the cache with transient merge-queue builds.\\n\\n### All CI test/build workflows\\n\\nAdded `merge_group:` to the `on:` trigger in:\\n- `build-toolchain.yml`, `binutils-tests.yml`, `gcc-selftests.yml`, `gdb-selftests.yml`, `libiberty-tests.yml`, `shell-unit-tests.yml`\\n\\nThe existing `check-changes` pattern already handles this correctly — `dorny/paths-filter` only runs on `pull_request`; for all other events (including `merge_group`) the `|| 'true'` fallback forces the main job to run.\\n\\n### `commitlint.yml`\\n\\nThree targeted changes:\\n\\n1. **Trigger**: added `merge_group: types: [checks_requested]`\\n2. **Checkout ref**: updated to `${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha || github.event.merge_group.base_sha }}` so the base branch's commitlint config is used in both contexts\\n3. **Validation**: split into two conditional steps — PR title on `pull_request`, head commit message on `merge_group`, using `printf '%s\\\\n'` for reliable input passing (avoids `echo` mangling strings starting with `-n` or platform-specific escape handling):\\n\\n```yaml\\n- name: Validate merge queue commit message\\n  if: github.event_name == 'merge_group'\\n  env:\\n    COMMIT_MSG: ${{ github.event.merge_group.head_commit.message }}\\n  run: printf '%s\\\\n' \\\"$COMMIT_MSG\\\" | npx --no-install commitlint --verbose\\n```\\n\\n### Read-only caches for `merge_group`\\n\\nAll `actions/cache` uses have been split into `actions/cache/restore` + `actions/cache/save` pairs. The save step is conditioned on `github.event_name != 'merge_group'` so merge-queue runs restore from the cache but never write back to it:\\n\\n- **`build-toolchain.yml`**: prerequisites cache, binutils stage cache, toolchain cache\\n- **`gcc-selftests.yml`**: GCC build cache\\n\\n`*.lock.yml` files are intentionally not modified (auto-generated).\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nWorkflow YAML syntax validated via CodeQL Actions analysis (0 alerts). The `check-changes` fallback behaviour for non-`pull_request` events is unchanged from existing logic.\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ----\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_title\\u003eUpdate all workflows to support a merge queue\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_description\\u003e- DO NOT update any `.github/workflow/**.lock.yml` files as they are generated\\n\\u003e - Update commitlint workflow / config to work with the commit queue\\n\\u003e   - Squash PR using commitlint compliant title\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ---\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003e **Note:** If this issue leads to a pull request, the **PR title** must follow\\n\\u003e \\u003e [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format, as required by this\\n\\u003e \\u003e repository's commitlint configuration (e.g. `feat: add support for Cortex-M55`).\\n\\u003e \\u003c/issue_description\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003ccomments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/comments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX --\\u003e\\n\\n- Fixes grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32#174\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS --\\u003e\\n---\\n\\n💡 You can make Copilot smarter by setting up custom instructions, customizing its development environment and configuring Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers. Learn more [Copilot coding agent tips](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips) in the docs.\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":