id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87IkkJz\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4035353146,\"number\":173,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"ci: update agentic workflows to align with gnu-tools-for-stm32 repository\",\"body\":\"The agentic workflow `.md` files were imported from generic templates containing instructions for Go, JavaScript, Python, and .NET projects — none of which apply here. Instructions are now written in terms of repository patterns rather than specific file names, so they stay accurate as the codebase evolves.\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n- **`code-simplifier.md`** — Replace four language-specific standards blocks (Go/JS/Python/.NET) with shell script and CI YAML conventions matching this repo. Validation commands now use the `tests/` discovery pattern (`for t in tests/test-*.sh`) and `bash -n` syntax checking.\\n\\n- **`daily-test-improver.md`** — Drop irrelevant network allowances (`dotnet`, `node`, `python`, `rust`, `java`). Task 1 cross-reference updated to describe patterns (CI workflow files in `.github/workflows/`, build scripts in repo root) rather than specific filenames.\\n\\n- **`plan.md`** — Remove the `cookie` label (template artefact). Fix `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md` reference (path doesn't exist) to point at `.github/copilot-instructions.md`. Fix stale inline comment: `max: 50` now correctly reads `# Maximum 50 sub-issues per group`.\\n\\n- **`shared/ci-optimization-strategies.md`** — Replace Go-specific `go test` analysis with the actual patterns of this repo: Phase 1 describes the three-job CI structure (`check-changes` → main → `\\u003cname\\u003e-status`), qualified to \\\"most test/build workflows\\\" with `commitlint.yml` noted as an intentional exception; Phase 2 describes cross-referencing `tests/test-*.sh` scripts against all workflow YAML files; Phase 3B reflects the `$(nproc)` build parallelism pattern. Restored \\\"Matrix strategy effectiveness\\\" as an explicit analysis bullet.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nDocumentation-only changes. Verified no specific file names remain hardcoded across all modified files. Verified factual accuracy of CI pattern claims against actual workflow files (e.g., confirmed `commitlint.yml` is a single-job workflow without the three-job pattern).\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ----\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_title\\u003eReview agentic workflows and bring in line with this repository\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_description\\u003e## Brief\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e The agentic workflows `.github/workflows/**.md` were imported from default templates and not all of the instructions are appropriate for this specific repository and its contents.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e **CRITICAL** Do not change the intent of the agentic workflows.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - Workflows brought in line with the specific needs of this repository\\n\\u003e - Do not modify the `.github/workflows/**.yml` files\\u003c/issue_description\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003ccomments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/comments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX --\\u003e\\n\\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#172\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS --\\u003e\\n---\\n\\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},\"comments\":2,\"closed_at\":\"2026-03-06T18:14:46Z\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-06T17:36:34Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-06T18:14:47Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/173\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/173\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/173/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/173/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/173/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32\",\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/173\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/173\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/173.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/173.patch\",\"merged_at\":\"2026-03-06T18:14:46Z\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/173/reactions\"},\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87Ij3Vs\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4032862449,\"number\":161,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"feat: add gcc-first stage cache restore/build/save triple with dedicated build script\",\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\nAdds a `restore → build → save` cache triple for the `gcc-first` (III-1) stage to `build-toolchain.yml`, following the identical pattern already used for `binutils`. This is the first incremental step toward per-stage caching (issue #142), deliberately split so `gcc-first` and `newlib` can be validated independently.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- **Restore cache – gcc-first**: Unconditional restore keyed on `steps.stage-hashes.outputs['gcc-first']` (bracket notation required for hyphenated output names; same `stage-v1-` prefix convention as binutils)\\n- **Build stage – gcc-first**: Gated on both `cache-gcc-first` and `cache-toolchain` not being hits; calls `./build-gcc-first.sh` directly (see below)\\n- **Save cache – gcc-first**: Same condition as build; captures cumulative `install-native` state through gcc-first\\n\\n- **`build-gcc-first.sh` (new)**: Standalone script containing only the gcc-first (III-1) build logic, extracted from `build-toolchain.sh` so that changes to other parts of the toolchain build do not invalidate the gcc-first stage cache. Accepts the same `--build_type` and `--skip_steps` flags as `build-toolchain.sh`; `--skip_stages` is accepted but ignored. Uses `cd \\\"$script_path\\\"` before sourcing `build-common.sh` to ensure `ROOT=$(pwd)` always resolves to the repo root. Does **not** wipe `install-native` — binutils output must already be present.\\n- **`build-toolchain.sh` – delegate gcc-first**: Inline gcc-first build block (~40 lines) replaced with `\\\"$script_path/build-gcc-first.sh\\\" \\\"$@\\\"` when the stage is not skipped.\\n- **`build-toolchain.yml` – stage hash isolation**: Added `gcc_first_scripts_hash` derived from `build-gcc-first.sh + build-toolchain-args.sh + build-common.sh`; `key_gcc_first` now uses `gcc_first_scripts_hash` so changes to `build-toolchain.sh` that don't touch `build-gcc-first.sh` or `build-toolchain-args.sh` no longer invalidate the gcc-first cache. `build-toolchain-args.sh` is included because `build-gcc-first.sh` sources it, so args parser changes could alter gcc-first behavior. Added `build-gcc-first.sh` to paths-filter.\\n- **`shell-unit-tests.yml`**: Added `build-gcc-first.sh` to paths-filter so unit tests run when the new script changes.\\n- **`build-toolchain.sh` fix 1 – preserve install-native on partial builds**: Guard `rm -rf $INSTALLDIR_NATIVE` at startup with `if [ \\\"x$skip_stages\\\" == \\\"x\\\" ]`. When `--skip_stages` is used (incremental partial build), `install-native` is no longer wiped at script startup, so restored predecessor-stage cache content (e.g., `arm-none-eabi/bin/` from the binutils cache restore) is preserved for the partial build. Full builds (no `--skip_stages`) continue to wipe `install-native` as before.\\n- **`build-toolchain.sh` fix 2 – skip III-11 specs on partial builds**: Guard the III-11 `specs` post-build step with `stage_is_skipped \\\"gcc-final\\\"`. The specs step enumerates multilib directories via `arm-none-eabi-gcc -print-multi-lib` and copies spec files into them, but those directories (e.g., `arm-none-eabi/lib/arm/v5te/softfp/`) are only created by `newlib`/`gcc-final`. When `gcc-final` is being skipped, the specs step now skips with a clear message instead of failing with `cp: No such file or directory`.\\n\\nThe three workflow steps are inserted after `Save cache – binutils` and before `Cache toolchain build`. When `src/gcc/` changes but `src/binutils/` is unchanged, the binutils cache hits and only gcc-first rebuilds.\\n\\n**Root cause of `build-toolchain.sh` fix 1:** Without the guard, `Build stage – gcc-first` would run with `--skip_stages=binutils,...`, which wiped `install-native` (destroying the just-restored binutils cache), then skipped binutils (so `arm-none-eabi/bin/` was never repopulated), then the post-build III-9 `strip_host_objects` step ran `find install-native/arm-none-eabi/bin/` which exited 1 under `set -e`.\\n\\n**Root cause of `build-toolchain.sh` fix 2:** After fix 1, the III-11 `specs` step was still reached. Its existing guard (`[ -x arm-none-eabi-gcc ]`) passes after gcc-first builds, but the multilib directories that `cp` targets only exist after `newlib` runs. Per `docs/build-stages.md`, specs depends on `gcc-final`; guarding with `stage_is_skipped \\\"gcc-final\\\"` correctly skips specs for any partial build that has not yet run gcc-final.\\n\\n**Note:** Because `build-gcc-first.sh` and `gcc_first_scripts_hash` inputs changed, the gcc-first stage cache is invalidated on the next CI run. Subsequent runs where only `build-toolchain.sh` changes (but not `build-gcc-first.sh` or `build-toolchain-args.sh`) will no longer invalidate the gcc-first cache.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- YAML validated syntactically via Python `yaml.safe_load`\\n- `--skip_stages` values verified against the validation whitelist in `build-toolchain.sh` (`binutils|gcc-first|newlib|newlib-nano|gcc-final|gcc-size-libstdcxx|gdb`)\\n- Both shell unit test suites pass (95 tests total: 36 in `test-build-common.sh` + 59 in `test-build-toolchain-args.sh`) after all `build-toolchain.sh` changes\\n- CodeQL analysis: 0 alerts\\n- Both CI failures reproduced and root causes confirmed via GitHub Actions job logs\\n- Confirmed `build-gcc-first.sh` sources `build-toolchain-args.sh` (line 59), validating inclusion in `gcc_first_scripts_hash`\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\n----\\n\\n*This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\n\\u003cissue_title\\u003e[plan] Add gcc-first stage cache restore/build/save triple to build-toolchain.yml\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003cissue_description\\u003e## Objective\\n\\nAdd a `restore → build → save` cache triple for the **`gcc-first`** (III-1) build stage in `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`, following the same pattern already used for the `binutils` stage.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThis is the first of two incremental steps to implement issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#142. The change has been deliberately split so that `gcc-first` and `newlib` can be validated independently — implementing both at once previously made debugging too difficult.\\n\\nThe `Compute stage source hashes` step already emits a `gcc-first` key via `steps.stage-hashes.outputs.gcc-first`. The `stage_is_skipped` logic in `build-toolchain.sh` supports `--skip_stages=binutils,...` to run only the `gcc-first` stage when its predecessors' outputs are already present in `install-native`.\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nInsert the following three steps **after** the `Save cache – binutils` step and **before** the `Cache toolchain build` step:\\n\\n```yaml\\n# --- Stage: gcc-first ---\\n- name: Restore cache – gcc-first\\n  id: cache-gcc-first\\n  uses: actions/cache/restore@[REDACTED] # v5.0.3\\n  with:\\n    path: install-native\\n    key: ${{ runner.os }}-stage-v1-${{ steps.stage-hashes.outputs.gcc-first }}\\n\\n- name: Build stage – gcc-first\\n  if: steps.cache-gcc-first.outputs.cache-hit != 'true' \\u0026\\u0026 steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\\n  run: |\\n    export JOBS=$(nproc)\\n    ./build-toolchain.sh \\\\\\n      --skip_steps=mingw,mingw-gdb-with-python,gdb-with-python,manual,package_sources \\\\\\n      --skip_stages=binutils,newlib,newlib-nano,gcc-final,gcc-size-libstdcxx,gdb\\n\\n- name: Save cache – gcc-first\\n  if: steps.cache-gcc-first.outputs.cache-hit != 'true' \\u0026\\u0026 steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\\n  uses: actions/cache/save@[REDACTED] # v5.0.3\\n  with:\\n    path: install-native\\n    key: ${{ runner.os }}-stage-v1-${{ steps.stage-hashes.outputs.gcc-first }}\\n```\\n\\n**Key implementation notes:**\\n\\n- Use the same actions/cache SHA already present in the workflow (`[REDACTED] # v5.0.3`).\\n- The `--skip_stages=binutils,...` argument tells `build-toolchain.sh` to skip the binutils stage and run only `gcc-first`. The binutils output must already be present in `install-native` (from the binutils cache triple that precedes this block).\\n- `steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit` is referenced before the `Cache toolchain build` step runs, so it evaluates to `''` at this point (which satisfies `!= 'true'`). This matches the same pattern already used in the binutils build/save steps. The condition will short-circuit properly if the monolithic cache later replaces this with a hit on a future run.\\n- The `cache-gcc-first` restore has no `if:` guard (unconditional restore), ensuring that a previously-cached `gcc-first` snapshot (which includes cumulative `install-native` state from binutils through gcc-first) is always preferred over rebuilding. The restore action is a no-op if the key is not found.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] The three new steps appear in the correct position in `build-toolchain.yml` (after `Save cache – binutils`, before `Cache toolchain build`)\\n- [ ] The cache key uses `stage-v1-` prefix and `steps.stage-hashes.outputs.gcc-first`\\n- [ ] The build step skips `binutils` (already done) and all stages after `gcc-first`\\n- [ ] The build and save steps share the same `if:` condition\\n- [ ] When `src/gcc/` changes but `src/binutils/` is unchanged: binutils cache hits, gcc-first miss triggers a build, save captures the new gcc-first state\\n- [ ] YAML is valid and the workflow lints cleanly\\n- [ ] The existing `binutils` cache triple is not modified\\nRelated to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#142\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003e Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22754576747) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#142 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/[REDACTED]/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@[REDACTED]\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e - [x] expires \\u003c!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-08T08:07:28.690Z --\\u003e on Mar 8, 2026, 8:07 AM UTC\\n\\n\\u003c!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22754576747, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22754576747 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --\\u003e\\u003c/issue_description\\u003e\\n\\n## Comments ...\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX --\\u003e\\n\\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#159\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS --\\u003e\\n---\\n\\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https:/