,{\"id\":4032854468,\"number\":158,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"ci: fix CI Optimization Coach prompt for this shell/C toolchain project\",\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\n`ci-coach.md` imported `shared/ci-data-analysis.md`, a module designed for the `gh-aw` Go/Node.js project. The compiled lock file injected incompatible setup steps that failed before the agent could start:\\n\\n- `Setup Node.js` with `cache-dependency-path: actions/setup/js/package-lock.json` — path doesn't exist → fatal npm cache error, all subsequent steps skipped\\n- `Setup Go` with `go-version-file: go.mod` — no `go.mod` here\\n- `make deps-dev/lint/build/recompile` — no `Makefile`\\n- `npm ci` in `./actions/setup/js` — directory doesn't exist\\n- Download runs for `ci.yml` — no such workflow in this repo\\n\\n**`ci-coach.md` fixes** (lock file must be regenerated via `gh aw compile` after merge):\\n\\n- **Remove `shared/ci-data-analysis.md` import** — eliminates all Go/npm setup steps on next compilation\\n- **Target workflows**: replace `ci.yml` with the six actual workflows (`build-toolchain.yml`, `binutils-tests.yml`, `gcc-selftests.yml`, `gdb-selftests.yml`, `libiberty-tests.yml`, `shell-unit-tests.yml`)\\n- **Data access**: replace stale pre-downloaded file references (`/tmp/ci-runs.json`, `/tmp/ci-artifacts/`, etc.) with instructions to use live GitHub MCP tools\\n- **Project context**: add explicit note that this is a shell/C toolchain — no `go.mod`, `Makefile`, or `actions/setup/js/`\\n- **Phase 2**: rewrite test-coverage analysis for this repo's actual test structure (shell + DejaGnu + selftests)\\n- **Phase 3**: remove fuzz-test optimisation items (no fuzz tests here)\\n- **Phase 5**: replace `make lint \\u0026\\u0026 make build \\u0026\\u0026 make test-unit \\u0026\\u0026 make recompile` with `bash tests/test-build-common.sh`; fix cache-memory path to `/tmp/gh-aw/cache-memory/`\\n- **Duplicates**: remove duplicated `## Data Available` and `### Phase 5` section headers\\n- **PR template example**: replace Go-specific `go test` restructuring example with a cache-key optimisation example relevant to this repo\\n\\n\\u003e ⚠️ `ci-coach.lock.yml` is auto-generated and must not be edited directly. Run `gh aw compile` (or trigger **Agentic Maintenance** → `upgrade`) after merging to regenerate the lock file from the corrected source.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- Verified `bash tests/test-build-common.sh` passes (28/28).\\n- Confirmed no remaining references to `ci.yml`, `make lint/build/test-unit/recompile`, `go.mod`, `go test`, `*_test.go`, `ci-data-analysis`, or stale `/tmp/ci-*` paths.\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003e [!WARNING]\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003csummary\\u003eFirewall rules blocked me from connecting to one or more addresses (expand for details)\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e #### I tried to connect to the following addresses, but was blocked by firewall rules:\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e - `https://api.github.com/graphql`\\n\\u003e   - Triggering command: `/usr/bin/gh gh auth status` (http block)\\n\\u003e - `https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/releases/latest`\\n\\u003e   - Triggering command: `/usr/bin/gh gh extension install github/gh-aw` (http block)\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e If you need me to access, download, or install something from one of these locations, you can either:\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e - Configure [Actions setup steps](https://gh.io/copilot/actions-setup-steps) to set up my environment, which run before the firewall is enabled\\n\\u003e - Add the appropriate URLs or hosts to the custom allowlist in this repository's [Copilot coding agent settings](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/settings/copilot/coding_agent) (admins only)\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\