rd-linked file: `assert_zero_exit` guards the call, link count drops from 2 → 1, content intact\\n- Add `trap 'rm -rf \\\"$_BHL_TMPDIR\\\"' EXIT` immediately after `mktemp -d` to ensure the temp directory is always cleaned up, even if `set -e` aborts the script early\\n- Wrap the bare `break_hardlink` invocation in the hard-link test with `assert_zero_exit` so failures are recorded as test failures rather than aborting the harness\\n\\nSubshell wrappers (`bash -c`) are used for error-path tests to prevent `error()`'s `exit 1` from aborting the test script.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n`bash tests/test-build-common.sh` — 36 passed, 0 failed (28 pre-existing + 8 new).\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ----\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_title\\u003e[aw] Daily Test Improver failed\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_description\\u003e### Workflow Failure\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e **Workflow:** [Daily Test Improver](https://github.com/githubnext/agentics/tree/[REDACTED]/workflows/daily-test-improver.md)  \\n\\u003e **Branch:** 13.3.rel1  \\n\\u003e **Run:** https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22751229687\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e **⚠️ Code Push Failed**: A code push safe output failed, and subsequent safe outputs were cancelled.\\n\\u003e **Code Push Errors:**\\n\\u003e - `create_pull_request`: Failed to apply patch\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ### Action Required\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e **Option 1: Assign this issue to Copilot**\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Assign this issue to Copilot using the `agentic-workflows` sub-agent to automatically debug and fix the