lot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},\"comments\":2,\"closed_at\":\"2026-03-06T08:12:12Z\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-06T07:50:04Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-06T08:12:13Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/157\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/157\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/157/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/157/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/157/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32\",\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/157\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/157\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/157.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/157.patch\",\"merged_at\":\"2026-03-06T08:12:11Z\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/157/reactions\"},\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87Ibb5K\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4031418728,\"number\":153,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"ci: add per-stage cache save/restore for binutils stage\",\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\nAdds the first per-stage `actions/cache` restore→build→save triple for the binutils stage (III-0) in `build-toolchain.yml`, establishing the pattern for subsequent stages.\\n\\n**`.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`:**\\n- **`Restore cache – binutils`** — `actions/cache/restore` keyed on `stage-hashes.outputs.binutils` (the cascading hash from the existing \\\"Compute stage source hashes\\\" step)\\n- **`Build stage – binutils`** — runs only on cache miss; uses `--skip_stages=gcc-first,newlib,newlib-nano,gcc-final,gcc-size-libstdcxx,gdb` to isolate the binutils build\\n- **`Save cache – binutils`** — `actions/cache/save` with the same key; guarded by the same cache-miss condition\\n\\nAll three steps are inserted between \\\"Compute stage source hashes\\\" and the existing monolithic \\\"Cache toolchain build\\\" step. The monolithic cache is left in place; both coexist until all stages have per-stage caches. Same `actions/cache` SHA (`[REDACTED]` / v5.0.3) as the rest of the workflow.\\n\\n**`build-toolchain.sh`** (bug fixes required by the new CI step): When `--skip_stages` is used to build only binutils, several post-build stages unconditionally attempted to access GCC-specific paths and binaries that do not exist in a binutils-only install. Fixed by guarding these operations with existence checks:\\n- **III-9** `strip_host_objects`: wrapped `find lib/gcc/arm-none-eabi/$GCC_VER/` in a `-d` directory existence check\\n- **III-10** `strip_target_objects`: wrapped the `.a` and `.o` `find` calls against `lib/gcc/arm-none-eabi/$GCC_VER` in a `-d` directory existence check\\n- **III-11** `specs`: wrapped `arm-none-eabi-gcc -print-multi-lib` in a `-x` executable existence check\\n- **III-12** `package_tbz2`: replaced the static `tar` argument list with a loop that only includes subdirectories (`arm-none-eabi`, `bin`, `lib`, `share`) that actually exist under `install-native/`; `lib` is explicitly deleted after binutils (III-0) and is absent until `gcc-first` repopulates it\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- YAML syntax validated.\\n- Logic verified against the stage hash computation and `build-toolchain.sh --skip_stages` valid values (`binutils|gcc-first|newlib|newlib-nano|gcc-final|gcc-size-libstdcxx|gdb`).\\n- Shell unit tests pass (28/28) after `build-toolchain.sh` changes.\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ----\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_title\\u003e[plan] Add per-stage cache save/restore for binutils stage in build-toolchain.yml\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_description\\u003e## Objective\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Add a per-stage `actions/cache` restore→build→save triple to `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml` for the **`binutils` stage** (III-0). This is the first and simplest stage — establishing the pattern that will be repeated for all remaining stages.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Context\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#75 describes replacing the single monolithic `install-native` cache with 7 per-stage caches. Each stage stores a cumulative snapshot of `install-native/` so restoring stage N gives you everything stages 0…N wrote.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e This issue covers only the `binutils` stage. The monolithic cache is left in place for now (it is removed in a later issue after all stages are covered). The two caches coexist temporarily; the per-stage cache provides a fast path for binutils-only changes.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Depends on:\\n\\u003e - grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#73\\n\\u003e - grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#74\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Approach\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e In `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`, between the prerequisites build step and the existing monolithic toolchain cache step, insert:\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ```yaml\\n\\u003e # --- Stage: binutils ---\\n\\u003e - name: Restore cache – binutils\\n\\u003e   id: cache-binutils\\n\\u003e   uses: actions/cache/restore@(SHA) # v4\\n\\u003e   with:\\n\\u003e     path: install-native\\n\\u003e     key: ${{ runner.os }}-stage-v1-${{ steps.src-hashes.outputs.binutils }}\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - name: Build stage – binutils\\n\\u003e   if: steps.cache-binutils.outputs.cache-hit != 'true' \\u0026\\u0026 steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\\n\\u003e   run: |\\n\\u003e     export JOBS=$(nproc)\\n\\u003e     ./build-toolchain.sh \\\\\\n\\u003e       --skip_steps=mingw,mingw-gdb-with-python,gdb-with-python,manual,package_sources \\\\\\n\\u003e       --skip_stages=gcc-first,newlib,newlib-nano,gcc-final,gcc-size-libstdcxx,gdb\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - name: Save cache – binutils\\n\\u003e   if: steps.cache-binutils.outputs.cache-hit != 'true' \\u0026\\u0026 steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\\n\\u003e   uses: actions/cache/save@(SHA) # v4\\n\\u003e   with:\\n\\u003e     path: install-native\\n\\u003e     key: ${{ runner.os }}-stage-v1-${{ steps.src-hashes.outputs.binutils }}\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Use the same `actions/cache` SHA already used in the file for the prerequisites cache.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Files to Modify\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - [ ] A clean run saves the `binutils` cache after building only the binutils stage\\n\\u003e - [ ] On a second run with unchanged `src/binutils/`, the `binutils` restore step hits and the Build stage – binutils step is skipped\\n\\u003e - [ ] If only `src/gdb/` changes (not `src/binutils/`), the `binutils` cache still hits (cascade hash is unchanged)\\n\\u003e - [ ] If `src/binutils/` changes, the `binutils` cache misses and rebuilds\\n\\u003e - [ ] YAML is valid, workflow lints cleanly\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Notes\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e This issue intentionally keeps the monolithic cache; both coexist. The monolithic cache is removed in a later issue once all stages have their own cache entries.\\n\\u003e Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#75, which is related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#71.\\n\\u003e Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#75\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003e Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22737048557) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#75 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\\n\\u003e \\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003e To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/[REDACTED]/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\\n\\u003e \\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003e gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@[REDACTED]\\n\\u003e \\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003e - [ ] expires \\u003c!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-07T21:24:20.808Z --\\u003e on Mar 7, 2026, 9:24 PM UTC\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22737048557, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22737048557 --\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan --\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --\\u003e\\u003c/issue_description\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003ccomments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/comments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX --\\u003e\\n\\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#141\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS --\\u003e\\n---\\n\\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},\"comments\":4,\"closed_at\":\"2026-03-06T07:21:25Z\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-06T00:21:51Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-06T07:21:28Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/153\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32\",\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/153\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/153\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/153.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/153.patch\",\"merged_at\":\"2026-03-06T07:21:25Z\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153/reactions\"},\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87IW_f2\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4030831436,\"number\":148,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"test: add shell unit tests for build-toolchain.sh argument parsing\",\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\nThe argument-parsing logic in `build-toolchain.sh` (covering `--skip_steps`, `--build_type`, `--skip_stages`, `--with-multilib-list`, and related flags) was untested and unsourceable without triggering a full toolchain build.\\n\\n**`build-toolchain-args.sh`** (new) — extracts argument parsing into a sourceable helper:\\n- `_toolchain_usage()` — usage text documenting all supported flags including `--skip_stages`\\n- `parse_toolchain_args()` — sets all defaults and parses/validates all flags using safe bash parameter expansion (no `echo | sed`); supports `--skip_steps`, `--skip_stages`, `--build_type`, and `--with-multilib-list`\\n\\n**`build-toolchain.sh`** — replaces the inline parsing block with:\\n```bash\\n. \\\"$script_path/build-toolchain-args.sh\\\"\\nparse_toolchain_args \\\"$@\\\"\\n```\\nAlso fixes a merge conflict where the `--skip_stages` validation block was calling the now-removed `usage` function; changed to `_toolchain_usage`.\\n\\n**`tests/test-build-toolchain-args.sh`** (new) — 59 test cases across 7 groups using the same plain-bash harness as `test-build-common.sh`:\\n- `--skip_steps` — all valid step names, comma→space conversion\\n- `--skip_stages` — all valid stage names, comma→space conversion\\n- `--build_type` — `native`, `ppa`, `debug`, combinations\\n- Defaults when no flags given (including `skip_stages`)\\n- `--with-multilib-list` parsing\\n- Multiple flags combined (including all 4 flags together)\\n- Error exits for unrecognised flag, bad `--build_type`, bad `--skip_steps`\\n\\n**`.github/workflows/shell-unit-tests.yml`** — runs both test scripts; adds `build-toolchain.sh` and `build-toolchain-args.sh` to the paths-filter.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n```\\nbash tests/test-build-common.sh              # 28 passed, 0 failed (unchanged)\\nbash tests/test-build-toolchain-args.sh      # 59 passed, 0 failed\\n```\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\u003e [!IMPORTANT]\\n\\u003e **PR title must follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format.**\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e PRs are squashed into the target branch using the **PR title** as the commit message.\\n\\u003e The PR title must therefore conform to commitlint requirements:\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003ctype\\u003e[(optional scope)][!]: \\u003cdescription\\u003e\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e Examples: `feat: add ARMv8-M support`, `fix: correct stack calculation`, `docs: update build instructions`\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e Individual commits **within** the PR do **not** need to follow this format.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ----\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_title\\u003e[plan] Add bats-core unit tests for build-toolchain.sh argument parsing\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_description\\u003e## Objective\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Add bats-core unit tests for the argument parsing logic in `build-toolchain.sh`, covering `--skip_steps`, `--build_type`, `--skip_stages`, and related flags.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Background\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 (Test Improver monthly activity) identified shell script unit testing as Priority 2. The argument parsing in `build-toolchain.sh` (~lines 85–155) handles multiple flags with complex semantics:\\n\\u003e - `--skip_steps=STEPS` — comma-separated list converted to space-separated string\\n\\u003e - `--build_type=` — controls native/mingw32/mingw-w64 builds\\n\\u003e - `--skip_stages=` — controls which toolchain stages to skip\\n\\u003e - Various boolean flags (`--ppa`, `--no-ppa`, etc.)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e This parsing is untested and failures could produce hard-to-debug broken builds.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Prerequisites\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e This issue depends on the bats-core setup established in the `saveenv`/`restoreenv` test issue. If bats-core is not yet added to the repo, follow the same approach chosen there.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Approach\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e 1. Isolate the argument-parsing logic for testing. The challenge is that `build-toolchain.sh` runs the full build when sourced. Options:\\n\\u003e    - Extract argument-parsing into a separate sourceable function/file (preferred, small refactor)\\n\\u003e    - Use `set -- (args)` and source only up to the argument parsing section with an early-exit guard\\n\\u003e 2. Create `test/build-toolchain-args.bats` with test cases:\\n\\u003e    - `--skip_steps=binutils,gcc` → `skip_steps` variable is `\\\"binutils gcc\\\"`\\n\\u003e    - `--skip_steps=` (empty) → `skip_steps` is empty\\n\\u003e    - `--build_type=mingw32` → `build_type` is set correctly\\n\\u003e    - `--skip_stages=III` → `skip_stages` is set correctly\\n\\u003e    - Unrecognised flag produces an error/usage message\\n\\u003e    - Multiple flags can be combined\\n\\u003e 3. Document how to run the tests.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Files to Create / Modify\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - Create: `test/build-toolchain-args.bats`\\n\\u003e - Modify: `build-toolchain.sh` (minimally, if extraction/guard is needed)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - [ ] At least 6 test cases covering argument parsing scenarios\\n\\u003e - [ ] Tests do not trigger an actual toolchain build when run\\n\\u003e - [ ] All tests pass on current `build-toolchain.sh`\\n\\u003e - [ ] Tests are runnable locally with a single command\\n\\u003e Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003e Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\\n\\u003e \\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003e To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/[REDACTED]/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\\n\\u003e \\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003e gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@[REDACTED]\\n\\u003e \\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003e - [x] expires \\u003c!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-07T01:31:10.104Z --\\u003e on Mar 7, 2026, 1:31 AM UTC\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22697787836, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836 --\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan --\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --\\u003e\\u003c/issue_description\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cagent_instructions\\u003eBefore starting to implement this issue first consider if the exisiting shell unit tests approach will be suitable for use with `build-toolchain.sh`.\\u003c/agent_instructions\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003ccomments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/comments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX --\\u003e\\n\\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#117\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS --\\u003e\\n---\\n\\n🔒 GitHub Advanced Security automatically protects Copilot coding agent pull requests. You can protect all pull requests by enabling Advanced Security for your repositories. [Learn more about Advanced Security.](https://gh.io/cca-advanced-security)\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},\"comments\":2,\"closed_at\":\"2026-03-06T13:59:57Z\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-05T21:50:14Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-06T13:59:59Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/148\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/148\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/148/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/148/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/148/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32\",\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/148\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/148\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/148.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/148.patch\",\"merged_at\":\"2026-03-06T13:59:57Z\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/148/reactions\"},\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87IVYAb\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4030566400,\"number\":138,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"ci: add per-stage cascade cache key computation\",\"body\":\"Adds a `stage-hashes` step to `build-toolchain.yml` that computes deterministic, cascading cache keys for each native build stage using `git rev-parse HEAD:\\u003cdir\\u003e` (O(1) tree-SHA lookup) instead of `hashFiles()` glob scanning the ~217k-file `src/` tree.\\n\\n### Key design\\n\\n- Each stage key hashes its own source directory SHA **chained to the prior stage's key**, giving cascade invalidation:\\n  - `src/binutils` change → invalidates `binutils` + all downstream keys\\n  - `src/gdb` change → invalidates only `gdb` + `final`\\n- `scripts_hash` captures `build-toolchain.sh` + `build-common.sh` so build-script changes invalidate all stages\\n- `prereqs_key` from the prerequisites cache step is included so prerequisite changes cascade through all stages\\n\\n### Outputs (via `${{ steps.stage-hashes.outputs.\\u003cname\\u003e }}`)\\n\\n`binutils` → `gcc-first` → `newlib` → `newlib-nano` → `gcc-final` → `gcc-size-libstdcxx` → `gdb` → `final`\\n\\nThese outputs are ready to be consumed by per-stage cache steps in subsequent work.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nStep logic validated via code review and CodeQL scan (0 alerts). Cascade invalidation properties verified by inspection of the key construction chain.\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\n----\\n\\n*This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\n\\u003cissue_title\\u003e[plan] Add cascade cache key computation step to build-toolchain.yml\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003cissue_description\\u003e## Objective\\n\\nAdd a workflow step that computes a per-stage source-tree hash for each native build stage using `git rev-parse HEAD:(dir) | sha256sum` (not `hashFiles`). These hashes feed into the cascade cache keys added in subsequent issues.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThe current single-toolchain cache key uses `hashFiles('src/binutils/**', 'src/gcc/**', ...)` on multiple large directories. On the ~217 k-file `src/` tree this can time out. The fix (consistent with the existing prerequisites cache pattern) is to use `git rev-parse HEAD:(dir)` which returns the tree object SHA instantly without walking all files.\\n\\nFor cascade invalidation each stage's cache key must include the source hash of that stage **and** the cache key of all prior stages. A cache key is just a string, so it can be computed incrementally with shell string concatenation and sha256sum.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nAdd a single new step **\\\"Compute stage source hashes\\\"** in `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`, placed after the prerequisites cache step and before the toolchain build step:\\n\\n```yaml\\n- name: Compute stage source hashes\\n  id: stage-hashes\\n  run: |\\n    hash_dir() { git rev-parse HEAD:\\\"$1\\\" 2\\u003e/dev/null || echo \\\"missing-$1\\\"; }\\n    scripts_hash=$(echo \\\"$(hash_dir build-toolchain.sh)$(hash_dir build-common.sh)\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\n    prereqs_key=\\\"${{ steps.cache-prerequisites.outputs.cache-primary-key }}\\\"\\n\\n    binutils_src=$(hash_dir src/binutils)\\n    gcc_src=$(hash_dir src/gcc)\\n    newlib_src=$(hash_dir src/newlib)\\n    gdb_src=$(hash_dir src/gdb)\\n    specs_src=$(hash_dir src/specs)\\n\\n    key_binutils=$(printf '%s' \\\"${{ runner.os }}-stage-binutils-${scripts_hash}-${prereqs_key}-${binutils_src}\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\n    key_gcc_first=$(printf '%s' \\\"${{ runner.os }}-stage-gcc-first-${scripts_hash}-${key_binutils}-${gcc_src}\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\n    key_newlib=$(printf '%s' \\\"${{ runner.os }}-stage-newlib-${scripts_hash}-${key_gcc_first}-${newlib_src}\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\n    key_newlib_nano=$(printf '%s' \\\"${{ runner.os }}-stage-newlib-nano-${scripts_hash}-${key_newlib}-${newlib_src}\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\n    key_gcc_final=$(printf '%s' \\\"${{ runner.os }}-stage-gcc-final-${scripts_hash}-${key_newlib_nano}-${gcc_src}\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\n    key_gcc_size=$(printf '%s' \\\"${{ runner.os }}-stage-gcc-size-libstdcxx-${scripts_hash}-${key_gcc_final}-${gcc_src}\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\n    key_gdb=$(printf '%s' \\\"${{ runner.os }}-stage-gdb-${scripts_hash}-${key_gcc_size}-${gdb_src}\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\n    key_final=$(printf '%s' \\\"${{ runner.os }}-stage-final-${scripts_hash}-${key_gdb}-${specs_src}\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\n\\n    {\\n      echo \\\"binutils=${key_binutils}\\\"\\n      echo \\\"gcc-first=${key_gcc_first}\\\"\\n      echo \\\"newlib=${key_newlib}\\\"\\n      echo \\\"newlib-nano=${key_newlib_nano}\\\"\\n      echo \\\"gcc-final=${key_gcc_final}\\\"\\n      echo \\\"gcc-size-libstdcxx=${key_gcc_size}\\\"\\n      echo \\\"gdb=${key_gdb}\\\"\\n      echo \\\"final=${key_final}\\\"\\n    } \\u003e\\u003e \\\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThese outputs are then referenced as `${{ steps.stage-hashes.outputs.binutils }}` etc. by the per-stage cache steps (see the next sub-issue).\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] The step runs in under 5 seconds (git tree-SHA lookup is O(1))\\n- [ ] Each output key is a deterministic hash string\\n- [ ] Changing `src/binutils/` changes the `binutils` key AND all downstream keys (gcc-first, newlib, ..., final)\\n- [ ] Changing `src/gdb/` only changes the `gdb` and `final` keys\\n- [ ] No `hashFiles()` calls on large `src/**` globs are introduced\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\nRelated to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#71. PR title convention: `ci: add per-stage cascade cache key computation`.\\nRelated to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#71\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003e Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22666393924) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#71 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/[REDACTED]/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@[REDACTED]\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e - [x] expires \\u003c!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-06T11:06:20.421Z --\\u003e on Mar 6, 2026, 11:06 AM UTC\\n\\n\\u003c!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Pla