github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/138\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32\",\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/138\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/138\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/138.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/138.patch\",\"merged_at\":\"2026-03-06T00:20:24Z\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138/reactions\"},\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87IUlhf\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4030472477,\"number\":137,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"ci: add .shellcheckrc and targeted suppressions for legacy-style shellcheck findings\",\"body\":\"~500 shellcheck findings across the three build scripts were all legacy-style noise, making it impossible to add shellcheck to CI without drowning real issues. This PR reduces warnings/errors to zero while fixing one real bug.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n### `.shellcheckrc` (new)\\n- `shell=bash` — eliminates SC2148 (missing shebang) on sourced scripts\\n- `disable=SC2034,SC2268,SC2016` — globally suppresses intentional patterns:\\n  - `SC2034`: env-var constants in `build-common.sh` are consumed by sourcing scripts\\n  - `SC2268`: historic `[ \\\"x$v\\\" = \\\"x\\\" ]` POSIX idiom, cosmetic-only churn to change\\n  - `SC2016`: deferred `$` expansion inside `eval` strings\\n\\n### Real bug fixed — SC2145 (`build-toolchain.sh`)\\n`${invalid[@]/#/\\\\\\\\n}` inside a double-quoted string mixes array elements with surrounding text as separate arguments. Changed to `${invalid[*]/#/\\\\\\\\n}`.\\n\\n### SC2155 fixed (`build-common.sh`)\\nSplit `local dir=$(...)` / `local tmp=$(...)` into separate declare/assign so `dirname`/`mktemp` non-zero exit codes are not masked by `local`'s always-zero exit.\\n\\n### Targeted inline suppressions\\n| Code | Count | Location | Rationale |\\n|------|-------|----------|-----------|\\n| SC1083 | 14 | `build-common.sh` `saveenvvar`/`restoreenv` | Intentional `eval \\\\${}` dynamic-variable pattern |\\n| SC2154 | 7 | `build-common.sh`, `build-toolchain.sh` | Variables assigned via `eval`; shellcheck can't trace |\\n| SC2046 | 5 | all three scripts | `$(dirname …)` / `$(basename …)` on controlled build paths |\\n| SC2207 | 1 | `build-common.sh` | Word-split array population intentional |\\n| SC2206 | 1 | `build-toolchain.sh` | Loop variable word-split intentional |\\n| SC2038 | 1 | `build-toolchain.sh` | macOS-only `find \\\\| xargs file` pipeline |\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `shellcheck --severity=warning` exits 0 with **0 warnings/errors** (down from 32; target ≤ 30)\\n- `bash -n` syntax check passes on all three scripts\\n- All 28 `tests/test-build-common.sh` unit tests pass\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ----\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_title\\u003e[plan] Add .shellcheckrc and targeted suppressions for legacy-style findings in build scripts\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_description\\u003e## Objective\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Add a `.shellcheckrc` configuration file and targeted inline `# shellcheck disable=` comments to suppress the ~500 legacy-style findings in the three build scripts, so that shellcheck can be added to CI without noise drowning real issues.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Background\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 (Test Improver monthly activity) identified ~514 shellcheck findings across `build-common.sh`, `build-toolchain.sh`, `build-prerequisites.sh`. After fixing the 2 real SC2145 errors (separate issue), the remaining findings are legacy style:\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e | Code   | Count | Description                                      | Category        |\\n\\u003e |--------|-------|--------------------------------------------------|-----------------|\\n\\u003e | SC2086 | 548   | Double-quote to prevent word splitting           | Legacy style    |\\n\\u003e | SC2034 |  50   | Variable assigned but never used                 | Often intentional in envvar-save scripts |\\n\\u003e | SC2102 |  21   | Ranges only match single chars in bracket exprs  | Legacy pattern  |\\n\\u003e | SC2268 |  18   | Unnecessary `x`-prefix comparison (`[ \\\"x$v\\\" ...`) | Legacy shell idiom |\\n\\u003e | SC1083 |  15   | Literal `{` or `}` outside arithmetic            | Quoting legacy  |\\n\\u003e | SC2006 |  11   | Use `$(...)` notation instead of backticks       | Style           |\\n\\u003e | SC2154 |   7   | Variable referenced but not assigned              | Often dynamic eval |\\n\\u003e | SC2046 |   5   | Quote word-split in command substitution          | Legacy style    |\\n\\u003e | SC2148 |   2   | No shebang (sourced scripts)                     | Not applicable  |\\n\\u003e | SC2016 |   2   | Single-quoted `$` expansion                     | Intentional     |\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Approach\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e 1. Add a `.shellcheckrc` at the repo root to set:\\n\\u003e    - `shell=bash` (avoids SC2148 on sourced scripts)\\n\\u003e    - Disable repo-wide legacy codes: `disable=SC2034,SC2268,SC2016`\\n\\u003e 2. For `SC2086` (unquoted variables): These scripts intentionally use word-splitting on paths — add per-file or per-region `# shellcheck disable=SC2086` where intentional, rather than a global suppression. Focus on the most common patterns.\\n\\u003e 3. For `SC2006` (backticks): These can be mechanically fixed with `sed`. Replace `` `expr ...` `` with `$(expr ...)` throughout.\\n\\u003e 4. For `SC1083`, `SC2046`, `SC2102`, `SC2154`, `SC2162`, `SC2155`: add targeted inline suppressions only where the pattern is intentional.\\n\\u003e 5. After changes, run `shellcheck build-common.sh build-toolchain.sh build-prerequisites.sh` and confirm finding count drops significantly.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Files to Create / Modify\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - Create: `.shellcheckrc`\\n\\u003e - Modify: `build-common.sh`, `build-toolchain.sh`, `build-prerequisites.sh` (inline suppressions where needed)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - [ ] `.shellcheckrc` exists and sets `shell=bash`\\n\\u003e - [ ] `shellcheck` finding count drops to ≤ 30 (warnings/errors only, not style)\\n\\u003e - [ ] No real bugs are suppressed — each suppression targets a demonstrably intentional pattern\\n\\u003e - [ ] `bash -n` syntax check still passes on all three scripts\\n\\u003e Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003e Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\\n\\u003e \\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003e To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/[REDACTED]/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\\n\\u003e \\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003e gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@[REDACTED]\\n\\u003e \\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003e - [ ] expires \\u003c!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-07T01:31:06.583Z --\\u003e on Mar 7, 2026, 1:31 AM UTC\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22697787836, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836 --\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan --\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --\\u003e\\u003c/issue_description\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003ccomments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003ccomment_new\\u003e\\u003cauthor\\u003e@grahame-white\\u003c/author\\u003e\\u003cbody\\u003e\\n\\u003e /plan how to incrementally fix these findings and remove the suppressions\\u003c/body\\u003e\\u003c/comment_new\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/comments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX --\\u003e\\n\\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#114\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS --\\u003e\\n---\\n\\n🔒 GitHub Advanced Security automatically protects Copilot coding agent pull requests. You can protect all pull requests by enabling Advanced Security for your repositories. [Learn more about Advanced Security.](https://gh.io/cca-advanced-security)\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"Copilot\",\"id\":198982749,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https:/