3301?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions\"},{\"login\":\"grahame-white\",\"id\":214149191,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODMOoRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/grahame-white\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORdWri87IUSL0\",\"draft\":false},{\"id\":4030233313,\"number\":123,\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"fix: replace $@ with $* in error/warning functions to fix SC2145\",\"body\":\"## Description\\n\\n`$@` inside a double-quoted string with surrounding text (e.g. `\\\"$0: error: $@\\\"`) silently drops all arguments after the first. `$*` joins all arguments with IFS into a single string — the correct behaviour for message-formatting functions.\\n\\n- **`build-common.sh` lines ~30 and ~37**: `\\\"$0: error: $@\\\"` → `\\\"$0: error: $*\\\"` and `\\\"$0: warning: $@\\\"` → `\\\"$0: warning: $*\\\"`\\n- **`build-common.sh` `error()` function**: Removed unreachable `set -u` that appeared after `exit 1`.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `shellcheck build-common.sh` — no SC2145 findings remain\\n- `bash -n build-common.sh build-toolchain.sh build-prerequisites.sh` — syntax check passes\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\u003e [!IMPORTANT]\\n\\u003e **PR title must follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format.**\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e PRs are squashed into the target branch using the **PR title** as the commit message.\\n\\u003e The PR title must therefore conform to commitlint requirements:\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003ctype\\u003e[(optional scope)][!]: \\u003cdescription\\u003e\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e Examples: `feat: add ARMv8-M support`, `fix: correct stack calculation`, `docs: update build instructions`\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003e Individual commits **within** the PR do **not** need to follow this format.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eOriginal prompt\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ----\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_title\\u003e[plan] Fix SC2145 shellcheck errors in build-common.sh (error/warning functions)\\u003c/issue_title\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cissue_description\\u003e## Objective\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Fix the two confirmed `(error)` severity shellcheck findings in `build-common.sh`. These represent genuine bugs, not legacy style issues.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Background\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Running `shellcheck build-common.sh` reports:\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e In build-common.sh line 30:\\n\\u003e     echo \\\"$0: error: $@\\\" \\u003e\\u00262\\n\\u003e                      ^-- SC2145 (error): Argument mixes string and array. Use * or separate argument.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e In build-common.sh line 37:\\n\\u003e     echo \\\"$0: warning: $@\\\" \\u003e\\u00262\\n\\u003e                        ^-- SC2145 (error): Argument mixes string and array. Use * or separate argument.\\n\\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e `$@` inside a double-quoted string with other text produces a single concatenated word for the first argument only, losing the rest. Using `\\\"$*\\\"` or `\\\"$@\\\"` standalone (with proper quoting) is the correct fix.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Approach\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e 1. In `build-common.sh`, locate the `error()` function (~line 30) and `warning()` function (~line 37).\\n\\u003e 2. Change `\\\"$0: error: $@\\\"` → `\\\"$0: error: $*\\\"` (and same for warning).  \\n\\u003e    `$*` joins all arguments with IFS into a single string, which is the intended behaviour for these message-formatting functions.\\n\\u003e 3. Run `shellcheck build-common.sh` to confirm the two errors are resolved.\\n\\u003e 4. Verify the scripts still function correctly by running `bash -n build-common.sh build-toolchain.sh build-prerequisites.sh`.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Files to Modify\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - `build-common.sh` — lines ~30 and ~37\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - [ ] `shellcheck build-common.sh` reports zero `(error)` severity findings\\n\\u003e - [ ] The `error()` and `warning()` functions still produce correct output (verified by manual inspection or a quick test)\\n\\u003e - [ ] `bash -n` syntax check passes on all three scripts\\n\\u003e Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003e Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\\n\\u003e \\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003e To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/[REDACTED]/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\\n\\u003e \\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003e gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@[REDACTED]\\n\\u003e \\u003e ```\\n\\u003e \\u003e - [x] expires \\u003c!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-07T01:31:05.512Z --\\u003e on Mar 7, 2026, 1:31 AM UTC\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22697787836, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836 --\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan --\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --\\u003e\\u003c/issue_description\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003ccomments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/comments\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX --\\u003e\\n\\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#113\\n\\n\\u003c!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS --\\u003e\\n---\\n\\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).